Feature: Therapeutic Area Study Aggregation and Analysis

  This feature aggregates study data by therapeutic area to provide insights into study progress and effectiveness. It calculates total studies, completed studies, ongoing studies, and average enrolled subjects per therapeutic area, and outputs results to the purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results table.

  Background:
    Given the source table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" exists in Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks" schema "purgo_playground"
    And the output table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results" exists with columns: therapeutic_area, total_studies, completed_studies, ongoing_studies, avg_enrolled_subjects
    And the column "study_conduct_status" may contain values such as "Completed", "Ongoing", "Terminated", "Withdrawn", "Suspended", "Planned", "Unknown"
    And the column "enrolled_subjects_qty" may contain null values
    And grouping is to be performed by "therapeutic_area"
    And "total_studies" is defined as the count of unique "study_title" per "therapeutic_area"
    And "completed_studies" is the count of studies where "study_conduct_status" = "Completed"
    And "ongoing_studies" is the count of studies where "study_conduct_status" = "Ongoing"
    And "avg_enrolled_subjects" is the average of "enrolled_subjects_qty" per "therapeutic_area", excluding nulls
    And duplicate "study_title" within a "therapeutic_area" is counted once for "total_studies"
    And only studies with non-null "therapeutic_area" and non-null "study_title" are included in the analysis

  Scenario: Aggregate study data for each therapeutic area (happy path)
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains valid data for multiple therapeutic areas
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the results table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results" should contain one row per therapeutic_area
    And each row should have:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
    And "total_studies" should be the count of unique "study_title" per therapeutic_area
    And "completed_studies" should be the count of studies with "study_conduct_status" = "Completed" per therapeutic_area
    And "ongoing_studies" should be the count of studies with "study_conduct_status" = "Ongoing" per therapeutic_area
    And "avg_enrolled_subjects" should be the average of "enrolled_subjects_qty" per therapeutic_area, excluding nulls

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven aggregation for multiple therapeutic areas
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" contains studies for <therapeutic_area>
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the results table should contain a row for <therapeutic_area> with:
      | therapeutic_area   | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
      | <therapeutic_area> | <total_studies> | <completed_studies> | <ongoing_studies> | <avg_enrolled_subjects> |

    Examples:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
      | Oncology         | 5             | 2                 | 3               | 120.0                 |
      | Cardiology       | 3             | 1                 | 2               | 85.5                  |
      | Neurology        | 4             | 3                 | 1               | 60.0                  |

  Scenario: Exclude studies with null therapeutic_area or study_title
    Given the table contains studies with null "therapeutic_area" or null "study_title"
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then studies with null "therapeutic_area" or null "study_title" should be excluded from all counts and averages

  Scenario: Handle null enrolled_subjects_qty in average calculation
    Given some studies have null "enrolled_subjects_qty"
    When calculating "avg_enrolled_subjects"
    Then only non-null "enrolled_subjects_qty" values should be included in the average
    And if all values are null for a therapeutic_area, "avg_enrolled_subjects" should be null

  Scenario: Handle duplicate study_title within a therapeutic_area
    Given multiple rows exist for the same "study_title" within a "therapeutic_area"
    When calculating "total_studies"
    Then "total_studies" should count each unique "study_title" only once per therapeutic_area

  Scenario: Error when source table is missing
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" does not exist
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then an error should be raised with message "Source table purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis not found"

  Scenario: Error when output table is missing
    Given the table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results" does not exist
    When attempting to write results
    Then an error should be raised with message "Output table purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results not found"

  Scenario: Ignore studies with status not in Completed or Ongoing for status counts
    Given studies exist with "study_conduct_status" values other than "Completed" or "Ongoing"
    When calculating "completed_studies" and "ongoing_studies"
    Then only studies with "study_conduct_status" = "Completed" are counted in "completed_studies"
    And only studies with "study_conduct_status" = "Ongoing" are counted in "ongoing_studies"
    And studies with other statuses are ignored for these counts

  Scenario: Output format validation
    Given the aggregation logic has completed
    When results are written to "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis_results"
    Then each row must have:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
    And "total_studies", "completed_studies", "ongoing_studies" must be bigint
    And "avg_enrolled_subjects" must be double or null

  Scenario: Data freshness requirement not specified
    Given no timeframe or data freshness filter is specified
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then all historical data in "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" should be included

  Scenario: No join or enrichment required unless specified
    Given no instruction to join with mapping tables or other enrichment sources
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then only data from "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" should be used

  Scenario: Exclude studies with missing data in required fields
    Given studies exist with missing "therapeutic_area" or "study_title"
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then these studies should be excluded from all calculations

  Scenario: Error when all enrolled_subjects_qty are null for a therapeutic_area
    Given all studies for a therapeutic_area have null "enrolled_subjects_qty"
    When calculating "avg_enrolled_subjects"
    Then "avg_enrolled_subjects" should be null for that therapeutic_area

  Scenario: Validate status mapping for completed and ongoing studies
    Given "study_conduct_status" values may include "Completed", "Ongoing", "Terminated", "Withdrawn", "Suspended", "Planned", "Unknown"
    When calculating "completed_studies" and "ongoing_studies"
    Then only "Completed" is mapped to "completed_studies"
    And only "Ongoing" is mapped to "ongoing_studies"
    And other statuses are ignored

  Scenario: Validate aggregation with mixed status and nulls
    Given the following data:
      | therapeutic_area | study_title | study_conduct_status | enrolled_subjects_qty |
      | Oncology         | Study A     | Completed            | 100                  |
      | Oncology         | Study B     | Ongoing              | 120                  |
      | Oncology         | Study C     | Terminated           | 110                  |
      | Oncology         | Study D     | Completed            | null                 |
      | Oncology         | Study E     | Ongoing              | 140                  |
      | Oncology         | Study A     | Completed            | 100                  |
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the results for Oncology should be:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
      | Oncology         | 5             | 2                 | 2               | 117.5                 |
    And "total_studies" counts unique study_title (Study A, B, C, D, E)
    And "completed_studies" counts studies with status "Completed" (Study A, Study D)
    And "ongoing_studies" counts studies with status "Ongoing" (Study B, Study E)
    And "avg_enrolled_subjects" averages non-null enrolled_subjects_qty (100, 120, 110, 140) = (100+120+110+140)/4 = 117.5

